<p class="wp-block-paragraph"><a href="https://www.relay.fm/focused/263">On this episode of <em>Focused</em></a>, Mike and I are joined by Cat Mulvihill to look at a frustrating productivity problem: having a good system and still not doing the work. Cat separates the reasons we get stuck into three categories, logical, biological, and psychological, because each one needs a different answer.</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">We talk about external accountability, ADHD and task initiation, perfectionism, and the tendency to keep rebuilding the system when the system isn&#8217;t the problem. Cat also explains Immunity to Change, a framework for finding the hidden fears and assumptions that can keep one foot on the brake.</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">Then we get into shiny new objects and what we&#8217;re reading. Cat&#8217;s Bluetooth home phone may be the best solution I&#8217;ve heard for keeping a cell phone out of the bedroom without missing an important family call.</p>



